---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Affiliate & Advertising Disclosure"
	description="Yeh Bro affiliate and advertising disclosure — commissions, /go/ links, what we never promote, and health information limits."
>
	<article class="prose-wrap">
		<p class="eyebrow">Policy</p>
		<h1>Affiliate &amp; Advertising Disclosure</h1>
		<p class="muted"><strong>Last updated:</strong> 2026-10-29</p>
		<p class="lede">
			Yeh Bro is an Australia-first fitness content brand (faceless, evidence-first natural lifter). We
			publish training and sports-nutrition guides and may earn money when you buy through links we
			recommend. Plain English — not formal legal advice. We aim not to mislead under Australian
			Consumer Law.
		</p>

		<h2>Affiliate links</h2>
		<p>
			Some links on this site and on our social channels are <strong>affiliate links</strong>. If you
			buy through them, Yeh Bro may earn a <strong>commission at no extra cost to you</strong>.
		</p>
		<p>
			We use tracked redirects such as <code>/go/[slug]</code> so we can update destinations when
			stock, shipping, or programs change. Product picks aim to fit an evidence-first Australian stack
			— typically creatine, protein, pre/intra, and basic vitamins — using label facts, dosing ranges,
			and AUD / shipping reality.
		</p>
		<p>
			We weigh evidence, label transparency, dosing clarity, AU availability, and value. We do not
			rank products solely because a network pays more. Recommendations are
			<strong>our own editorial judgment</strong> unless a post clearly states a paid partnership or
			gifted product (#ad / branded-content disclosure).
		</p>

		<h2>What we do not promote</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Illegal anabolic-androgenic steroids (AAS)</li>
			<li>Restricted SARMs, unapproved peptides, or underground-lab gear</li>
			<li>“Cycle,” “blast,” or PCT product funnels that imply unlawful supply</li>
			<li>
				Prescription medicines without authority, or grey imports that breach Australian customs /
				TGA rules
			</li>
			<li>Guaranteed muscle or fat-loss results from supplements alone</li>
			<li>Fake “lab tested by us” claims or invented certifications</li>
		</ul>
		<p>Public summary: legal sports nutrition and training content only.</p>

		<h2>Health information</h2>
		<p>
			Nothing on Yeh Bro is <strong>medical advice</strong>, diagnosis, or treatment. Content is
			general information about training and sports nutrition. Speak to a qualified health
			professional about your situation before changing diet, training, or supplements — especially if
			you are pregnant, under clinical care, or have a medical condition.
		</p>

		<h2>Advertising &amp; fairness</h2>
		<p>
			We aim to be clear when a commercial relationship exists (affiliate, gifted, or paid). Paid
			partnerships will be labelled “Sponsored” or “Paid partnership.” Day-to-day affiliate links use
			on-page disclosure notes and this page.
		</p>
		<p>
			Prices and stock change; always check the retailer page on the day you buy. Comparisons use
			stated criteria and dates where we rank options — we avoid empty “best in Australia” claims
			without a basis.
		</p>

		<h2>Australia / ACL</h2>
		<p>
			We aim for clear, non-misleading claims. If something looks wrong,
			<a href="/contact">contact us</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Questions</h2>
		<p>
			Contact: <a href="mailto:hello@yehbro.com.au">hello@yehbro.com.au</a> or
			<a href="/contact">/contact</a>.
		</p>
		<p class="muted">Full voice and offer scope: Australia-first · phase-1 legal sports nutrition.</p>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>
